                "ImageDescription": {
                  "value": "Set up camp on an island for the Great American Campout tonight! #mypubliclandsroadtrip\nThe BLM Eastern States manages about 500 islands in Wisconsin and northeastern Minnesota. The unique island habitat and wildlife provide endless opportunities for photography and birdwatching, from the boat or shore. Many of these public islands are lesser known and visited recreational treasures, making them perfect for those looking for tranquil and peaceful camping environments. Find a quiet fishing spot on a smaller island; then camp overnight for a stunning sunrise over the water.",
